WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.036 --> 00:00:19.899
love horseback riding, Grace," Daisy said.

2
00:00:20.539 --> 00:00:21.400
Kaleem nodded.

3
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.382
"It's so fun!"

4
00:00:27.726 --> 00:00:30.088
The kids were walking toward Our Little Farm.

5
00:00:30.856 --> 00:00:34.639
Jan and Jon had invited them to meet some new animals and go riding.

6
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.622
Beatrice sat quietly on Daisy's headband.

7
00:00:39.383 --> 00:00:40.543
Grace bit her lip.

8
00:00:41.484 --> 00:00:43.266
"Riding seems scary."

9
00:00:43.286 --> 00:00:46.748
"Maybe at first," Kaleem said.

10
00:00:46.768 --> 00:00:48.329
"But you'll get used to it.

11
00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.472
Daisy and I ride on the beach during our vacation."

12
00:00:52.773 --> 00:00:53.593
Daisy nodded.

13
00:00:53.613 --> 00:00:54.934
"I can't wait.

14
00:00:55.475 --> 00:00:56.716
Summer will be here soon!"

15
00:01:00.904 --> 00:01:03.285
Jan and Jon waved as the kids approached.

16
00:01:03.305 --> 00:01:11.328
"Come meet our new pig, Hubert," Jon said, leading everyone to a new pigpen.

17
00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.611
Hubert's trying to get out!"

18
00:01:16.971 --> 00:01:17.671
Kaleem said.

19
00:01:19.932 --> 00:01:21.533
Jon rushed to close the gate.

20
00:01:21.553 --> 00:01:26.535
"He escaped twice yesterday.

21
00:01:27.675 --> 00:01:29.516
I guess I'd better fix the gate today."

22
00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:30.976
He sighed.

23
00:01:30.996 --> 00:01:34.697
"I was hoping to plant vegetables instead.

24
00:01:35.117 --> 00:01:36.978
There's so much to do on this farm!"

25
00:01:36.998 --> 00:01:40.199
"I can help you while the girls ride," Kaleem said.

26
00:01:40.219 --> 00:01:42.659
"Really?" Jon said.

27
00:01:42.679 --> 00:01:44.100
"That would be great!"

28
00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.540
"Sure," Kaleem said.

29
00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.021
"I've never fixed a pigpen or planted vegetables before.

30
00:01:50.721 --> 00:01:51.542
It'll be interesting."

31
00:01:52.282 --> 00:01:54.803
Beatrice suddenly buzzed in Daisy's ear.

32
00:01:54.823 --> 00:01:59.744
"A vegetable garden does sound interesting.

33
00:02:00.336 --> 00:02:01.756
I think I'll stay with Kaleem."

34
00:02:01.776 --> 00:02:04.237
"Okay," Daisy said.

35
00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:05.377
"See you later."

36
00:02:06.378 --> 00:02:08.038
Grace suddenly glanced over.

37
00:02:08.058 --> 00:02:10.419
"Who are you talking to?"

38
00:02:11.299 --> 00:02:13.280
Daisy laughed.

39
00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:16.581
"Myself! I do that sometimes."

40
00:02:24.563 --> 00:02:28.364
Jan led the girls to another stable, where four horses were tied.

41
00:02:30.272 --> 00:02:35.495
"We have a new horse named Sunny and a new pony named Blossom," Jan said.

42
00:02:39.097 --> 00:02:39.958
is so pretty!"

43
00:02:40.398 --> 00:02:41.178
Daisy said.

44
00:02:41.859 --> 00:02:42.639
Jan nodded.

45
00:02:42.659 --> 00:02:46.241
"He's called a palomino because of his golden coat."

46
00:02:47.442 --> 00:02:48.262
Sunny whickered.

47
00:02:48.282 --> 00:02:49.503
"Hi there.

48
00:02:49.923 --> 00:02:50.423
I'm new!"

49
00:02:51.264 --> 00:02:53.145
Daisy went over to pat Sunny.

50
00:02:53.165 --> 00:02:55.766
"I'm Daisy," she whispered.

51
00:02:55.786 --> 00:02:58.428
"I can understand you when you talk."

52
00:03:00.516 --> 00:03:01.796
Sunny flicked his tail.

53
00:03:01.816 --> 00:03:04.517
"Whoa! That's great!"

54
00:03:05.397 --> 00:03:06.738
Daisy turned to Jan.

55
00:03:06.758 --> 00:03:08.838
"Can I ride Sunny today?"

56
00:03:08.858 --> 00:03:12.679
"Sorry, no," Jan said.

57
00:03:12.699 --> 00:03:14.580
"He's young and green."

58
00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:18.341
"Green?" Grace looked confused.

59
00:03:18.361 --> 00:03:21.282
"I thought you said he was a palomino!"

60
00:03:22.642 --> 00:03:23.442
Jan laughed.

61
00:03:24.983 --> 00:03:28.384
"We call a horse 'green' when he's not fully trained yet.

62
00:03:30.684 --> 00:03:34.046
A horse dealer talked us into trying Sunny out for a while.

63
00:03:34.506 --> 00:03:37.428
But Jon thinks it will take too long to train him."

64
00:03:38.628 --> 00:03:39.449
She looked sad.

65
00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:44.712
"Jon wants to send Sunny back when the dealer returns today to check on him."

66
00:03:45.812 --> 00:03:47.113
Sunny whinnied gently.

67
00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:48.894
"I don't want to go back.

68
00:03:49.414 --> 00:03:50.194
I like it here."

69
00:03:50.214 --> 00:03:53.436
"I'll try to help you," Daisy whispered.

70
00:03:53.456 --> 00:03:56.978
"I just need to figure out how to change Jon's mind."

71
00:03:56.998 --> 00:04:00.240
"How about this, girls?"

72
00:04:00.692 --> 00:04:01.372
Jan said.

73
00:04:01.392 --> 00:04:05.093
"I'll give you a riding lesson before we go on a trail ride."

74
00:04:05.113 --> 00:04:08.874
"I've never ridden before," Grace said.

75
00:04:08.894 --> 00:04:11.295
"Can I ride the slowest horse?"

76
00:04:11.315 --> 00:04:15.436
"Sure. You can ride Blossom," Jan said.

77
00:04:15.456 --> 00:04:18.017
"She's very gentle with beginners.

78
00:04:19.017 --> 00:04:21.718
Sunny is better for more experienced riders."

79
00:04:21.738 --> 00:04:25.239
"I've ridden a lot," Daisy blurted out.

80
00:04:25.619 --> 00:04:27.679
"I've been on lots of different horses at the beach.

81
00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:29.640
All sizes too!"

82
00:04:30.712 --> 00:04:33.016
"Really?" Jan said in surprise.

83
00:04:33.036 --> 00:04:35.499
"I didn't know that, Daisy."

84
00:04:36.581 --> 00:04:37.562
Daisy looked down.

85
00:04:38.563 --> 00:04:41.828
She'd actually gone on only a few short beach rides.

86
00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:44.091
"Uh-oh," she thought.

87
00:04:44.111 --> 00:04:47.156
"I just told Jan a big, fat lie!"
